uired` while any decision\n      it waits on is pending. The IH-04 case of BUG-2026-09-29T190000 has the same cause for a requirements revision.\n    evidence: >\n      Found by the fast-check campaign on the kernel, confirmed by the four commands above on the real decider. Older\n      than the branch e38s04, which only replays the kernel. No application path issues a protocol revision today\n      (BUG-2026-10-09T171124), so only a direct kernel command reaches it; G5 still accepts c2 when evaluated, and the stale\n      request shows as pending until then.\n    risk_level: low\n    follow_ups: >\n      Withdraw the pending decisions about the candidate when the protocol is revised, with its own test, then remove the\n      exclusion from `ReviseProtocol` in `test/support/change-commands.ts`.\n    status: open\n0\nid: BUG-2026\nid: BUG-2026\nid: BUG-2026\n58:const EXIT_OF: Record<TlcOutcome, number> = { completed: 0, counterexample: 1, inconclusive: 2, error: 3 };\n59-\n60-function sha256Of(path: string): string {\n61-\treturn `sha256:${createHash(\"sha256\").update(readFileSync(path)).digest(\"hex\")}`;\n--\n294:process.exit(EXIT_OF[report.outcome]);","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"40929494-c108-4c84-aa96-67d3b7cd12e3","uuid":"132c2be1-a847-499b-bcc3-d0bf31d7984c","timestamp":"2026-10-09T18:37:41.022Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"bugs:\n  - bug_id: BUG-2026-09-27T170100\n    date: \"2026-09-27\"\n    title: \"G1 accepts a mandatory requirement's satisfied_by_reference claim without evidence, before G2/G5 are known to catch a false one\"\n    severity: medium\n    priority: p2\n    scope: domain\n    what_happened: >\n      A material answer bound to a mandatory requirement passes G1 (`gateG1`, `src/domain/change/decide.ts`)\n      as soon as the requirement is named, is mandatory, and the binding is observable — G1 never reads\n      `satisfied_by_reference`. A specification report can mark a brand-new, never-implemented\n      requi